Ladybird learns which sites are behind DataDome from the x-datadome
header on their responses, and presents the WebKit engine’s browser on
the platform to them: Safari’s User-Agent on macOS, WebKitGTK’s
elsewhere (Source/WebCore/platform/glib/UserAgentGLib.cpp
buildUserAgentString(), whose Version/60.5 token is deliberate), with
the WebKit navigator compatibility mode, remembered per site in the
profile. No engine presents another engine’s browser to a bot-detection
service; the nearest relatives are the static per-site User-Agent
overrides of Firefox’s webcompat add-on
(browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/interventions.js) and WebKitGTK’s
UserAgentQuirks::quirksForURL(), both hand-curated lists that add a
browser token for a site that blocks the browser’s own, and Chromium’s
WebContents::SetUserAgentOverride(), which its embedder drives. None of
the three changes the navigator’s engine along with the name, since
each already is the engine it names.
